## 2. Model Routing Table

All inference goes through the `@google/generative-ai` SDK (already installed at `^0.24.1`). Use these models:

| Capability | Model ID | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Text generation** (chat, quiz gen, flashcard gen, study plans, tutor, reranking) | `gemini-2.0-flash-lite` | Fast, cheap. Used for all structured text output. |
| **Image generation** | `gemini-2.0-flash-exp` (Imagen via Gemini) | Gemini's native image generation endpoint. Exact model slug TBD — use `gemini-2.0-flash-exp` with `responseModalities: ['IMAGE']` or the Imagen 3 endpoint if the SDK supports it. Verify SDK support before implementing. |
| **Audio / TTS** | `gemini-2.5-pro-preview-tts` | Text-to-speech. Subject to change for cheaper alternatives. Wrap in an abstraction so the model ID is easily swappable. |
| **Embeddings** (RAG pipeline) | `gemini-embedding-exp-03-07` (or current `text-embedding-004`) | **No functional change needed** — embeddings already route through Gemini via [getEmbedding()](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#203-250) in [client.ts](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts). Simply ensure the env var `GEMINI_API_KEY` is now the new key value. The embedding model and code path remain as-is. |

