## 3. Refactoring Plan — File-by-File

### 3.1 [src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts) (PRIMARY — Breaking Change)

This is the central AI client module. It currently exports `kiloClient`, [getChatCompletion](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#52-120), [streamChatCompletion](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#132-202), [getCandidateKiloModels](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#121-131), [isKiloConfigured](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#31-35), [getEmbedding](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#203-250), and `geminiClient`.

**Changes:**

1. **Remove** all Kilo-related code:
   - Delete `KILO_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY` constants
   - Delete the `_kiloClient` / `kiloClient` OpenAI SDK instance
   - Delete `KILO_CHAT_MODEL`, [getCandidateKiloModels()](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#121-131)
   - Delete [isKiloConfigured()](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#31-35)

2. **Remove** the `openai` npm dependency import. After migration, the `openai` package can be uninstalled from [package.json](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/package.json).

3. **Rewrite [getChatCompletion()](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#52-120)** to use the Gemini SDK:
   ```typescript
   import { GoogleGenerativeAI } from '@google/generative-ai';

   const GEMINI_API_KEY = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;
   const geminiClient = GEMINI_API_KEY ? new GoogleGenerativeAI(GEMINI_API_KEY) : null;

   const GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL = process.env.GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL || 'gemini-2.0-flash-lite';

   export async function getChatCompletion(
     messages: ChatMessage[],
     options?: ChatCompletionOptions,
   ): Promise<string> {
     if (MOCK_MODE_ENABLED) { /* existing mock logic */ }
     if (!geminiClient) throw new Error('GEMINI_API_KEY not configured');

     const model = geminiClient.getGenerativeModel({
       model: GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL,
       generationConfig: {
         temperature: options?.temperature ?? 0.7,
         maxOutputTokens: options?.maxTokens ?? 4096,
       },
     });

     // Convert ChatMessage[] to Gemini's format:
     // - system message → systemInstruction
     // - user/assistant → contents array with role 'user'/'model'
     const systemMsg = messages.find(m => m.role === 'system');
     const chatMessages = messages
       .filter(m => m.role !== 'system')
       .map(m => ({
         role: m.role === 'assistant' ? 'model' : 'user',
         parts: [{ text: m.content }],
       }));

     const chat = model.startChat({
       history: chatMessages.slice(0, -1),
       ...(systemMsg ? { systemInstruction: systemMsg.content } : {}),
     });

     const lastMsg = chatMessages[chatMessages.length - 1];
     const result = await chat.sendMessage(lastMsg.parts[0].text);
     const text = result.response.text();
     if (!text) throw new Error('No content returned from Gemini');
     return text;
   }
   ```

4. **Rewrite [streamChatCompletion()](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#132-202)** to use Gemini's streaming API:
   ```typescript
   export async function streamChatCompletion(
     messages: ChatMessage[],
     options?: { temperature?: number; maxTokens?: number },
   ): Promise<ReadableStream<Uint8Array>> {
     if (!geminiClient) throw new Error('GEMINI_API_KEY not configured');

     const model = geminiClient.getGenerativeModel({
       model: GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL,
       generationConfig: {
         temperature: options?.temperature ?? 0.7,
         maxOutputTokens: options?.maxTokens ?? 4096,
       },
     });

     // Same message conversion as above...
     const result = await chat.sendMessageStream(lastMsg.parts[0].text);

     // Convert Gemini's AsyncIterable to a web ReadableStream<Uint8Array>
     const encoder = new TextEncoder();
     return new ReadableStream({
       async start(controller) {
         for await (const chunk of result.stream) {
           const text = chunk.text();
           if (text) controller.enqueue(encoder.encode(text));
         }
         controller.close();
       },
     });
   }
   ```
   > **Important**: The return type changes from [Response](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/app/api/chat/tutor/route.ts#55-60) to `ReadableStream<Uint8Array>`. Update all call sites accordingly (see §3.3).

5. **Rename exports** for clarity:
   - [isKiloConfigured()](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#31-35) → `isAIConfigured()` (checks `!!GEMINI_API_KEY`)
   - Export `GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL` for debug routes

6. **[getEmbedding()](file:///c:/Projects/ApplicationDevelopment/Exam-Killer/src/shared/lib/openai/client.ts#203-250)** — Minimal change:
   - Remove the OpenAI/Kilo fallback branch (lines 234–246). Only Gemini path + mock remain.
   - The Gemini embedding path (lines 214–232) stays as-is.

7. **Export a new `isAIConfigured()` function:**
   ```typescript
   export function isAIConfigured(): boolean {
     return !!GEMINI_API_KEY;
   }
   ```

